copyListenT -- a copy starts with no listeners (Tony, 2026-11-25; SEQ 783). Listeners belong to the field, not to its
value or its attributes, so copyOf and copyDeep give the copy none; copyOf still shares the original's attributes.

Row by row, in pop.sh:
  CL-1 the copies carry no listener list: A's list is 2 (its attribute and its listener list), each copy's is 1.
       Before the cure each copy's was 2.
  CL-2 a write to the copyOf, and to the copyDeep, fires none of A's listeners and leaves A's value alone.
       Before the cure each write fired A's listener once.
  CL-3 A's listeners still fire, once per write to A, after both copies were made; the copies do not move.
  CL-4 control: copyOf shares A's attributes (a write through the copy reaches A, 40) and copyDeep does not (A stays 40,
       the copy reads 50).
  CL-5 every level of a copyDeep: a listened-to child inside a copied parent. A write to the copy's child fires nothing
       and the child keeps its value; a write to the child fires its listener.
NOT COVERED, and why: a listener added to the copy. listenTo names its field in a define, and a copy held by a holder has
no name a define can reach (listenTo:=theHolder listens to the holder). CL-1 pins what a fresh listener depends on: the
copy holds no listener list of A's to add to.
